# Settings the image fixes for every PC it is imported on. install-user.sh exports
# them for the build's own start.sh run; finalize-root.sh writes them into .env, so
# the first start on a PC sees the same values the build did.
#
# start.sh otherwise allows the machine's LAN address in the Vite server and folds
# it into the frontend build's fingerprint. Under WSL's default NAT networking that
# address is a VM address that only this PC can reach and that usually changes when WSL
# restarts, so every first start and every start after `wsl --shutdown` rebuilt the
# frontend (about a minute and up to 6 GB of memory for `vite build`). localhost is
# what the Windows browser uses; the machine's own hostname stays allowed by
# vite.config.js. With mirrored networking, add the PC's LAN address here in .env
# to reach the studio from other devices.
VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost
